        {
          "ruleId": "SUDO-GTFO-002",
          "message": {
            "text": "The user(s) [deploy] can run '/usr/bin/systemctl restart nginx.service' via sudo as [root] without a password (NOPASSWD) with the 'shell' capability. This enables immediate privilege escalation.\nGTFObins Context: Inherits shell behavior from less (and transitively via less -\u003e vi).\nNote: Pager escape requires a TTY with paged output and is typically restricted on systemd \u003e= 247 (LESSSECURE=1 under sudo) unless PAGER/SYSTEMD_PAGER/LESSSECURE is preserved or overridden.\nLaunching 'vi' from piped 'less' output requires opening a file first (e.g. ':e /path/to/file' then 'v').\nNote: Environment-variable techniques (e.g. LESSOPEN/VISUAL/EDITOR) require SETENV or matching env_keep permissions.\nIt might happen that the service is not started with '--now', in such cases it might be necessary to manually start it.\nThe optional 'reset' command is needed to receive the echo back of the typed keystrokes.\nRemediation: Remove this binary from sudoers or replace it with a tightly scoped wrapper script.\nExample Fix:\n# Replace direct 'systemctl' (shell) access with a root-owned wrapper script (EXEC: required when global Defaults noexec is active):\ndeploy ALL = (root) PASSWD: EXEC: sha256:\u003cdigest\u003e /usr/local/sbin/safe-systemctl-wrapper.sh \"\""
          },
