          "message": {
            "text": "The command '/usr/bin/cat /var/log/*' allowed for user(s) [ops] contains wildcards. Arguments matching wildcards in sudoers can often be bypassed using directory traversals (e.g. '/var/log/../../etc/shadow') or option injection.\nRemediation: Avoid wildcards in command paths. Use specific paths or write wrapper scripts that validate inputs before executing commands.\nExample Fix:\nops ALL = (root) /usr/bin/cat /var/log/explicit_target"
