          "ruleId": "SUDO-CMD-015",
          "message": {
            "text": "The rule at docs/examples/policy/sudoers.d/20-ops:6 for user(s) [backup] on host(s) [ALL] as [root] granting '/usr/local/sbin/backup.sh \"\"' shadows or overrides the earlier rule at docs/examples/policy/sudoers.d/20-ops:5 ('/usr/local/sbin/backup.sh \"\"'). Because sudoers evaluates matching rules using last-match-wins semantics, the later rule weakens security controls (PASSWD -\u003e NOPASSWD).\nRemediation: Consolidate overlapping sudoers entries so each principal, host, runas target, and command has a single unambiguous rule without unintended last-match-wins overrides.\nExample Fix:\n# Consolidate overlapping rules (docs/examples/policy/sudoers.d/20-ops:5 and docs/examples/policy/sudoers.d/20-ops:6) into a single explicit rule:\nbackup ALL = (root) PASSWD: NOEXEC: NOSETENV: /usr/local/sbin/backup.sh \"\""
