          "ruleId": "SUDO-CMD-013",
          "message": {
            "text": "The administrator-grade rule for user(s) [root] on host(s) [ALL] running as [ALL : %ALL] does not specify the 'TYPE=' and 'ROLE=' options. Without an explicit SELinux type and role transition, commands executed via sudo run in the invoking user's SELinux context instead of the administrator domain.\nRemediation: Add 'TYPE=sysadm_t ROLE=sysadm_r' to the administrator rule so sudo transitions to the SELinux administrator domain (DISA STIG V-272484 / RHEL-08-010455). On hosts not running SELinux this finding is informational and can be disregarded.\nExample Fix:\nroot ALL = (ALL : %ALL) TYPE=sysadm_t ROLE=sysadm_r ALL"
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/examples/policy/sudoers"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 8
                }
              }
            }
          ],
